{% comment %}
  Two tubs, two flavours, one Add To Cart.

  The flavour swatch block sells one tub: pick a flavour, the variant input
  follows, one line goes in the cart. This block sells a fixed pair — the
  shopper chooses a flavour for the first tub and a flavour for the second, and
  the single basket press puts one of each in the cart as two `items[n]` entries.
  That is the same mechanism the supply add-on already uses, so the cart request
  is one this section has been sending for a while.

  Size is not a choice here. The pair is locked to one value of the supply
  option — the 30-day tub on the Labor Day page — because the offer is about
  flavour variety, not quantity. Every swatch therefore resolves to the variant
  at (that flavour, the locked supply), and a product with no supply option at
  all simply resolves on flavour alone.

  Both rows default to a real selection rather than to nothing, so the block is
  never in a state where Add To Cart is dead on arrival. Left unset that default
  is the first flavour with stock; typing a flavour into a row's Default setting
  overrides it, which is how the two rows can start on different flavours.

  The total is an estimate and says so. The second-tub discount is an automatic
  discount held in Shopify, which the storefront cannot read at render time — so
  the percentage here is typed by the merchant and the note under the figure
  tells the shopper the real discount lands at checkout. Keep the two in step: a
  change to the store's automatic discount has to be repeated in this block.

  When the two rows land on the same flavour the cart merges them into one line
  at quantity two. That is deliberate — no line-item property is written that
  would force them apart, because two identical tubs on two lines reads as a
  bug to the shopper and to whoever picks the order.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the flavor_duo block.
  - product {Object} - product whose variants are paired; blank in preview.
  - current_variant {Object} - unused for selection, kept for signature parity.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-flavor-duo__block', block: block, product: product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign flavor_name = block.settings.flavor_option | strip | downcase
  assign supply_name = block.settings.supply_option | strip | downcase

  assign flavor_position = 0
  assign supply_position = 0

  for product_option in product.options_with_values
    assign this_name = product_option.name | strip | downcase
    if flavor_name != blank and this_name == flavor_name
      assign flavor_position = product_option.position
      assign flavor_values = product_option.values
    endif
    if supply_name != blank and this_name == supply_name
      assign supply_position = product_option.position
      assign supply_values = product_option.values
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if product != blank and flavor_position > 0 and flavor_values.size > 0 -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign flavor_key = 'option' | append: flavor_position

    comment
      The supply option's own spelling of the typed size.

      Merchants type "30-day supply"; the option holds "30-Day Supply", and the
      variant match below is case-sensitive because that is how Shopify stores
      option values. So the typed string only ever finds the real value, and the
      real value is what filters the variants — the same rule the size block
      follows.

      A typo falls back to the option's first value rather than to no lock at
      all: an unmatched size would otherwise leave every supply in the match set
      and let a swatch resolve to a 90-day tub, which is the one thing this
      block exists to prevent.
    endcomment
    assign supply_locked = ''
    if supply_position > 0
      assign supply_key = 'option' | append: supply_position
      assign wanted_supply = block.settings.supply_value | strip | downcase | replace: '-', ' '

      for option_value in supply_values
        assign this_value = option_value | strip | downcase | replace: '-', ' '
        if this_value == wanted_supply
          assign supply_locked = option_value
        endif
      endfor

      if supply_locked == blank
        assign supply_locked = supply_values.first
      endif
    endif

    comment
      The flavour both rows fall back to. Stock first, because a row that opens
      on a sold-out flavour presents the shopper with a dead button and no
      indication of which swatch would fix it.
    endcomment
    assign first_available = ''
    for flavor_value in flavor_values
      assign candidates = product.variants | where: flavor_key, flavor_value
      if supply_position > 0
        assign candidates = candidates | where: supply_key, supply_locked
      endif
      assign candidates_in_stock = candidates | where: 'available', true
      if candidates_in_stock.size > 0 and first_available == blank
        assign first_available = flavor_value
      endif
    endfor
    if first_available == blank
      assign first_available = flavor_values.first
    endif
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Each row's opening flavour, resolved the same loose way the size is: the
    merchant types a flavour, the option holds the spelling. Written out as text
    and split back apart because Liquid has no way to collect two resolved
    strings out of a loop.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign row_numbers = '1,2' | split: ',' -%}

  {%- capture row_defaults -%}
    {%- for row_number in row_numbers -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign default_key = 'row' | append: row_number | append: '_default'
        assign typed_default = block.settings[default_key] | strip | downcase
        assign resolved_default = ''

        if typed_default != blank
          for flavor_value in flavor_values
            assign this_value = flavor_value | strip | downcase
            if this_value == typed_default
              assign resolved_default = flavor_value
            endif
          endfor
        endif

        if resolved_default == blank
          assign resolved_default = first_available
        endif
      -%}
      {{- resolved_default -}}~|~
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign defaults = row_defaults | split: '~|~'
    assign default_1 = defaults[0] | strip
    assign default_2 = defaults[1] | strip

    comment
      The opening total, rendered here rather than left to the script, so the
      figure is correct in the first paint and on a page whose JavaScript never
      arrives. The script recomputes it from the same rule on every change.
    endcomment
    assign opening_1 = product.variants | where: flavor_key, default_1
    assign opening_2 = product.variants | where: flavor_key, default_2
    if supply_position > 0
      assign opening_1 = opening_1 | where: supply_key, supply_locked
      assign opening_2 = opening_2 | where: supply_key, supply_locked
    endif
    assign opening_cents_1 = opening_1.first.price | default: 0
    assign opening_cents_2 = opening_2.first.price | default: 0

    assign discount_pct = block.settings.second_discount | default: 0

    comment
      Against the cheaper of the two, which is how Shopify's own automatic
      discounts pick their target when a rule applies to one of a pair. On a
      product whose flavours are all one price it makes no difference; on one
      where they are not, it is the estimate that cannot overstate the saving.
    endcomment
    assign cheaper_cents = opening_cents_1 | at_most: opening_cents_2
    assign opening_list = opening_cents_1 | plus: opening_cents_2
    assign opening_saving = cheaper_cents | times: discount_pct | divided_by: 100.0 | round
    assign opening_now = opening_list | minus: opening_saving
  -%}

  <div
    class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo"
    data-cwc-duo
    data-cwc-duo-discount="{{ discount_pct }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {% if block.settings.label != blank %}
      <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-heading">{{ block.settings.label }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {%- for row_number in row_numbers -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign label_key = 'row' | append: row_number | append: '_label'
        assign badge_key = 'row' | append: row_number | append: '_badge'
        assign row_label = block.settings[label_key]
        assign row_badge = block.settings[badge_key]

        if row_number == '1'
          assign row_default = default_1
        else
          assign row_default = default_2
        endif
      -%}

      <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-row" data-cwc-duo-row="{{ row_number }}">
        <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-row-head">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__label">
            {{ row_label | default: 'Choose a flavor' }}
          </span>
          {% if row_badge != blank %}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-badge">{{ row_badge }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavors cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-swatches">
          {%- for flavor_value in flavor_values -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign matches = product.variants | where: flavor_key, flavor_value
              if supply_position > 0
                assign matches = matches | where: supply_key, supply_locked
              endif
              assign in_stock = matches | where: 'available', true
              assign swatch_variant = in_stock.first | default: matches.first

              comment
                The escape hatch: a variant id typed into the block wins over
                everything resolved above, for the case where the option values
                cannot express which variant a swatch should buy. It is looked
                up on the product rather than trusted as a bare number, so the
                price and the stock state stay real — an id that belongs to no
                variant of this product falls back to the resolved one.
              endcomment
              assign id_key = 'id_' | append: forloop.index
              assign typed_id = block.settings[id_key] | strip
              if typed_id != blank
                comment
                  Coerced to a number before the match: the setting is a text
                  field, variant ids are integers, and Liquid's where compares
                  the two by type as well as by value.
                endcomment
                assign typed_id_number = typed_id | plus: 0
                assign override_matches = product.variants | where: 'id', typed_id_number
                if override_matches.size > 0
                  assign swatch_variant = override_matches.first
                endif
              endif

              assign image_key = 'image_' | append: forloop.index
              assign swatch_image = block.settings[image_key] | default: swatch_variant.image

              assign color_key = 'color_' | append: forloop.index
              assign swatch_accent = block.settings[color_key]
              if swatch_accent == 'none'
                assign swatch_accent = blank
              endif
            -%}

            {%- if swatch_variant != blank -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor{% if flavor_value == row_default %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor--selected{% endif %}{% unless swatch_variant.available %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor--unavailable{% endunless %}"
                data-cwc-duo-option
                data-cwc-duo-variant="{{ swatch_variant.id }}"
                data-cwc-duo-value="{{ flavor_value | escape }}"
                data-cwc-duo-cents="{{ swatch_variant.price }}"
                data-cwc-duo-available="{{ swatch_variant.available }}"
                {% unless swatch_variant.available %}
                  disabled
                {% endunless %}
                {% if swatch_accent != blank %}
                  style="--flavor-accent: {{ swatch_accent }};"
                {% endif %}
              >
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-swatch{% if swatch_image == blank %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-swatch--empty{% endif %}">
                  {% if swatch_image != blank %}
                    <img
                      src="{{ swatch_image | image_url: width: 100 }}"
                      alt="{{ flavor_value | escape }}"
                      width="100"
                      height="100"
                      loading="lazy"
                    >
                  {% else %}
                    <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-empty-label">Image</span>
                  {% endif %}
                </span>
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__flavor-name">{{ flavor_value }}</span>
              </button>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- if block.settings.show_total -%}
      <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total" data-cwc-duo-total>
        <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-row">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-label">
            {{ block.settings.total_label | default: 'Your 2-tub bundle' }}
          </span>
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-figures">
            {%- comment -%}
              Struck-out list price and discount chip are hidden together when
              there is no discount to state, the way the price row does it: a
              strikeout with nothing beside it reads as a rendering fault rather
              than as a full-price bundle.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span
              class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-list"
              data-cwc-duo-total-list
              {% if opening_saving == 0 %}
                style="display: none;"
              {% endif %}
            >
              {{- opening_list | money -}}
            </span>
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-now" data-cwc-duo-total-now>
              {{- opening_now | money -}}
            </span>
          </span>
        </div>

        <div
          class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-total-note"
          data-cwc-duo-total-note
          {% if opening_saving == 0 %}
            style="display: none;"
          {% endif %}
        >
          {{ block.settings.discount_note
            | default: 'Second tub discount is applied automatically at checkout.'
          }}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The out-of-stock line. Empty until the script finds a row sitting on a
      flavour that has sold out since the page was cached, which is the only way
      a shopper reaches a dead Add To Cart from here.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__duo-error" data-cwc-duo-error role="alert"></div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
